Fraudulent Practices
Consultants shall not-
Collude with the other businesses and organizations with the intention of depriving a PDE of the benefits of free and open competition;
Enter into business arrangements that might prevent the effective conclusion of a procurement or disposal process in a fair manner;
Engage in deceptive financial practices, such as bribery, double billing or other improper financial practices;
Misrepresent or conceal facts in order to influence a procurement and disposal process or the execution of a contract to the detriment of the PDE; or utter false documents;
Unlawfully obtain information relating to a procurement and disposal process in order to influence the process or execution of a contract to the detriment of the PDE; and
Withhold from giving information to the PDE during contract execution to the detriment of the PDE.

